+- Existing acceptance examiners remain protected. The owner MUST NOT weaken, skip or delete them. A necessary change to an existing examiner requires a bounded written justification tied to the original criterion, preserves the original failing/acceptance evidence, and receives independent scrutiny. An existing examiner that contradicts the accepted criterion is a stop condition until the allowed correction is established.
+- The independent Critic remains a separate fresh-context evaluator. Its review of test changes looks for weakening (threshold lowering, assertion removal, skips) and for whether new regression tests exercise the reported behavior.
